  "document": {
    "abstract": "This technical recommendation describes the various configurations of cinematographic sound reproduction that use \"multichannel\" management, from monophonic tracks up to 8.1 tracks. It specifies:\n The physical distribution of the channels in the cinema auditorium\n The correspondence of the AES pairs used to record the sound tracks in digital format in exhibition DCP copies\n The reference naming of each of the pairs",
    "abstract$meta": {
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "English translation of the publisher's French text",
      "originalValue": null,
      "reviewRequired": true,
      "source": "inferred",
      "sourceUrl": "https://cst.fr/download/33/recommandations-techniques/986/cst-rt-022.pdf",
      "updated": "2026-10-02T16:10:02.304Z",
      "version": "extractDocs.js@commit:41a6e931279b"
    },
    "abstractOriginal": "La présente recommandation technique décrit les différentes configurations de la reproduction sonore cinématographique utilisant les possibilités de la gestion « multicanal », depuis les pistes monophoniques jusqu’aux pistes 8.1. Elle précise :\n La répartition physique des canaux dans la salle de cinéma\n La correspondance des paires AES utilisées pour l’enregistrement des pistes sonores au format numérique dans les copies DCP d’exploitation\n Le nommage de référence de chacune des paires",
    "abstractOriginal$meta": {
      "confidence": "high",
      "note": "Read from the publisher's document or website",
      "originalValue": null,
      "source": "parsed",
      "sourceUrl": "https://cst.fr/download/33/recommandations-techniques/986/cst-rt-022.pdf",
      "updated": "2026-10-02T16:10:02.304Z",
      "version": "extractDocs.js@commit:41a6e931279b"
    },
    "details": "French-language CST recommendation (2011) giving AES pair/channel assignments, labels and loudspeaker layouts for DCP cinema sound from mono to 8.1, including 7.1 ISO and 7.1 Dolby Surround. HI (hearing-impaired) and VI (audio description) tracks go on AES pair 4, and the document notes the conflict this creates with the ISO 7.1/8.1 layouts.",
